        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/crazy-taxi-world-tour-germany-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/crazy-taxi\">Crazy Taxi</a> was not my favourite Dreamcast game (please don't ask me to choose between the triumphant rhythm triptych of <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/rez\">Rez</a>, Space Channel 5, and <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/games/samba-de-amigo\">Samba de Amigo</a>, however), but there's a specific bit of it that's forever seared into my brain: the giddy thrill of cresting over that one San-Francisco-inspired hill and barreling down toward the ocean, all while The Offspring's All I Want 'Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah'ed me into a state of gaming nirvana.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/crazy-taxi-world-tour-gamescom-preview\">Read more</a></p>",
